  "checks": [
    "Standalone search produces an immutable native collection in one scan. Limit 0 stores no records; a positive limit stores only the first N; the total always covers the full range. A retained read-only sequence survives closing the snapshot and editing the source Buffer.",
    "Native raw and owned collectors agree on matching/capture offsets, including embedded NUL, zero-width matches, ordering, unmatched capture cells, and the full count. The Windows and Linux hosted/static C tests run at O0 and O2 and inject allocation failures during collection growth. Live allocation and invalid/double free counters remain unchanged.",
    "Single-match replacement uses the existing native producer and matched-XRT owned bytes admission. The fixtures check an inner NUL copied from a regex capture, exact bytes, empty inputs and results, and preservation of the previous bytes value after a failure.",
    "The language behavior fixture and window-free learning example pass real CLI JIT and standalone dynamic/static AOT; public emitted declarations compile as C11, C++11 and C++17. The standalone binaries do not import a compiler library. The separate performance fixture runs in JIT.",
    "With prebuilt snapshots and an acquired sequence, 1000 C and xlang iterations each sum the same 15000 captured byte offsets and perform no XRT allocation, reallocation or free. The benchmark excludes snapshot allocation, search, sequence admission and release; native record reads and ordinary lifetime checks remain."
  ]
